<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-26683] IndexQuery uses index before data population completes; should throw &#8220;index not found&#8221;</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-26683</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;During the initial build, IndexQuery treats an initialized-but-unpopulated index as available. Align with the SQL engine: return &#8220;index not found&#8221; until the index&#8217;s data population completes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
